Lowercase 'one' is strongest after prepositions, especially 'from'.
Determiners weaken it; adjective-modified noun substitutes are negative.
Verb objects are stronger, particularly after -ing forms. Capitalized forms
are weaker. Smaller rules cover 'a single', 'at once', and plural 'ones'.
Repeated middle dots have a separate negative response. Other vocabulary
and distant context are not modeled.
